[claude] 🔧 mcp__kernelgen__finalize_round: {"conclusion": {"round_num": 1, "expectation_status": "baseline", "root_cause": "Baseline established: single fused in-place Triton pass fixes the three INCORRECT_NUMERICAL strided cases of the FlagGems seed (30/30 PASSED). Perf is limited by host-side Triton JIT dispatch, not by device work: every tiny case (N=1024) measures 72.0-78.0 us while the 16.7M-element cases measure only 83.5-85.2 us, so ~55 us of per-call Python/JIT dispatch dominates every workload.", "perf_gap_analysis": "No previous measurement (baseline). Absolute view: correctness is now complete; latency is essentially flat across four orders of magnitude of N (72 us at N=1024 vs 84 us at N=16777216), which localises the cost in the kernel[grid](...) dispatch path rather than in memory traffic. Reference latencies are 10.5-11.8 us on the tiny cases, so the headroom there is pure launch cost.", "next_suggestion": "Resolve the compiled Triton launcher once per (dtype, numel) and invoke it directly with grid + raw stream + device pointer, removing the per-call JIT binder/cache-key work; keep the ordinary kernel[grid](...) launch as the fallback for masked-free/misaligned/debug-profiling cases. Expected effect: tiny cases approach the ~16 us launch floor already demonstrated by the in-place negative_ reference, and the large cases shed the same fixed overhead.", "optimization_level": "L1_architecture", "knowledge_assessments": []}}
